# Exemplar: a generic relationship card (a `per: npc` cast), from content/events/social.grim,
# with its queued follow-up. Why it works: pronoun tokens make it fit anyone; the cast says who the
# premise fits (a peer: someone your age you'd lend rent money to), not just who it excludes; the loan
# trades gold for friendship with a chance it never comes back; the follow-up is queued "with npc" so
# the same person repays you two months later, with three variants of how. Amounts are tiers;
# "fifteen crowns" in the text is what `gold medium` is in @balance (lint checks that they match).

@event soc_borrow_money
title: A Small Loan
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and rel(npc) >= 3
per: npc
trigger: social
when: gold >= 20
repeat: 6
art: pouch
tags: social money
scene: A student holding out an empty purse upside down with a sheepish grin.
text: {npc} turns out an empty purse. "I'm fifteen crowns short {~for rent|for the term's ink and parchment|for the wand-mender, and it's my only wand}. I'll pay you back. I swear on my wand."
> left: Sorry, you're tight too
  rel npc -small
  say: "No, of course, I understand." {They} {are} quiet at dinner.
> right: Lend fifteen crowns
  gold -medium
  alignment +tiny
  rel npc +medium
  chance likely:
    queue soc_loan_repaid in 2 with npc
    say: {npc} hugs you with the empty purse still in {their} hand.
  else:
    say: {npc} hugs you. You suspect you will never see those fifteen crowns again.

@event soc_loan_repaid
title: Paid Back
class: story
tone: light
trigger: queued
actor: npc
art: coin
tags: social money
scene: A small stack of coins and a sweet bun left on a desk with a thank-you note.
text: {~{npc} finds you after class and presses a little stack of coins into your hand, plus a sticky bun. "Fifteen crowns. And interest." The interest is the bun.|{npc} turns up at breakfast with a small purse and a very straight face. "Fifteen crowns. I said I would."|{npc} slides fifteen crowns across the library table, one coin at a time. The last one has a note under it: "Thank you. Really."}
> left: Count it
  gold +medium
  rel npc +small
  mood +tiny
  say: You count it, because {they}'d be offended if you didn't. Fifteen exactly. {npc} nods, satisfied, as if a debt of honour has been settled.
> right: Pocket it without counting
  gold +medium
  rel npc +small
  mood +tiny
  say: You put it away uncounted. {npc} looks quietly pleased to be trusted, which was worth more than the crowns.
